        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Glinka, Jean-Baptiste Lully, Alexey Verstovsky\n- Roles: composer, instrumentalist, dancer, musical bureaucrat\n- Places: Russia, France\n- Organizations: court of Louis XIV of France\n- Concepts: Russian classical music\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully was born Giovanni Battista Lulli on 28 November 1632 and died on 22 March 1687.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully was an Italian-born French composer, instrumentalist, and dancer who spent most of his life working at the court of Louis XIV of France.\n- Alexey Verstovsky was born on 1 March 1799 old style 18 February and died on 17 November 1862 old style 5 November.\n- Mikhail Glinka was born on 1 June 1804 old style 20 May and died on 15 February 1857 old style 3 February.\n- Mikhail Glinka was the first Russian composer to gain wide recognition within Russia and is often regarded as the fountainhead of Russian classical music.\n- Alexey Verstovsky was a Russian composer and musical bureaucrat who was a rival of Mikhail Glinka.",
